WEBVTT

01:03.229 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:17.160 --> 01:18.870
Please, don't, don't.

01:18.953 --> 01:20.330
I want to live.

01:20.413 --> 01:24.542
You're asking for mercy
with the hands that pushed Ka-young?

01:25.543 --> 01:28.671
Your murdering hands deserve no mercy.

01:40.433 --> 01:44.354
I've confirmed his existence.
But you are now a widow, Mother.

01:45.730 --> 01:46.981
I say good riddance.

01:47.816 --> 01:50.777
I wonder, do you think
he saved Ki Ka-young,

01:50.860 --> 01:53.071
or do you think she used a wish?

01:53.154 --> 01:54.322
That level of fury…

01:55.281 --> 01:56.866
suggests it's not a wish.

02:10.755 --> 02:12.715
Father!

02:15.051 --> 02:18.930
You've lived a thousand years, but still
you act like such a fool, Khalid!

02:20.431 --> 02:24.269
You should be so grateful that Iblis
didn't let her use up her final wish.

02:24.352 --> 02:27.272
If that had indeed been her last wish,

02:27.355 --> 02:32.026
I could then claim the lamp as my own
and be the ultimate master.

02:32.110 --> 02:33.319
Who do you think you are?

02:34.028 --> 02:37.115
All of that girl's wishes
have been for the sake of others,

02:37.657 --> 02:41.327
and her final wish
must be a righteous one as well.

02:42.245 --> 02:46.374
It's under my control.
Iblis will succumb to his inevitable fate.

02:47.709 --> 02:50.420
Therefore that means
he will never serve anyone new.

02:50.503 --> 02:51.588
He'll be damned by my hand.

02:52.338 --> 02:54.883
So, even if the lamp's
present master dies,

02:55.675 --> 02:57.385
I cannot have the lamp for myself?

02:57.969 --> 02:59.971
You are merely half a genie.

03:00.889 --> 03:04.184
Do not anger me. Do not interfere
in what does not concern you!

03:04.267 --> 03:07.562
I am Ejllael. My destiny is to kill Iblis.

03:08.605 --> 03:12.442
This is your absolute
final warning, Khalid.

03:25.121 --> 03:26.372
-Father!
-Look!

03:37.300 --> 03:38.801
Is your master okay?

03:39.552 --> 03:41.095
She took a few sleeping pills.

03:42.263 --> 03:44.974
Sade, there's somewhere I have to go.

03:45.934 --> 03:48.061
I'll need you to stand guard over her
while I'm gone.

03:48.811 --> 03:52.440
This means, you're allowed to use
your beast powers today.

03:53.816 --> 03:54.692
Yes, Master.

04:44.826 --> 04:47.328
It's been a long time, brother.

04:48.913 --> 04:51.457
I haven't seen you since our battle days.

04:55.878 --> 04:59.799
It seems your garden
has grown a little sad.

05:01.050 --> 05:01.926
Hasn't it?

05:02.010 --> 05:04.095
You forget that you were the reason

05:04.178 --> 05:06.139
for the garden spoiling
in the first place.

05:06.681 --> 05:10.143
Yes, well, I was all the way
on the front line

05:10.226 --> 05:13.354
of our great war,
with you all the way in the back.

05:13.438 --> 05:15.440
Quiet! Why have you come here?

05:19.027 --> 05:21.195
Do you have any foreign flowers?

05:21.779 --> 05:23.614
If I am blessed

05:23.698 --> 05:27.076
with some foreign seeds
brought by the wind, I plant them.

05:28.494 --> 05:29.370
Satisfied?

05:31.581 --> 05:34.792
So, do you have any foreign seeds

05:34.876 --> 05:38.212
that the wind brought all the way
from the East in 1040 AD?

05:40.298 --> 05:45.011
If so, when did the flowers fall
and the seeds get redistributed?

05:45.094 --> 05:46.095
Oh.

05:46.971 --> 05:50.600
You want to fill an empty void
in your mind, don't you?

05:53.561 --> 05:55.813
What do you suppose actually happened?

06:12.580 --> 06:13.498
Khalid!

06:16.793 --> 06:19.629
It seems the cough has worsened.
Are you feeling all right, Khalid?

06:20.630 --> 06:24.092
You never get sick,
nor can you die, Father.

06:24.175 --> 06:28.137
I have nothing to do
but weave these unbreakable threads.

06:29.055 --> 06:32.975
This incessant weakness
is too much to endure.

06:33.059 --> 06:35.853
Why did you have me
knowing I'd have such weaknesses?

06:37.647 --> 06:39.982
Sickness and mortality
are the law of life.

06:41.275 --> 06:45.071
But this limitation can be a blessing.
Mortals live their lives more diligently.

06:45.154 --> 06:48.032
It's not fair. You're an immortal being.

06:48.616 --> 06:52.245
And yet, you can't do anything
for your son who will one day die.

06:52.328 --> 06:53.996
All you can offer me is an apple.

07:01.421 --> 07:04.257
Hey, you! Thief! Catch him!

07:04.340 --> 07:06.717
He stole that bread! Seize that boy!

07:09.554 --> 07:11.139
Got you!

07:11.222 --> 07:12.557
You scoundrel!

07:12.640 --> 07:14.267
I'll show you. Little thief!

07:14.350 --> 07:17.019
You think you can steal? I'll teach you
a lesson you won't forget.

07:17.603 --> 07:18.438
Stop!

07:21.149 --> 07:23.526
He is just a child
and he is starving to death.

07:24.902 --> 07:27.864
If you aren't going to pay for the bread,
do not interfere.

07:37.331 --> 07:39.542
Come on, eat this.

07:42.879 --> 07:47.383
How strange. You seem to have
an immortal spirit or something.

07:49.886 --> 07:51.387
It's not my fault, sir.

07:58.644 --> 08:00.271
So Shadi changed their souls.

08:16.662 --> 08:19.457
Did Shadi contain
his sick son's mortal spirit

08:21.000 --> 08:22.543
within an eternal body?

08:22.627 --> 08:24.295
I helped Shadi do so.

08:25.421 --> 08:27.340
And I was punished severely for it.

08:31.636 --> 08:33.846
The worst punishment I could fathom.

08:35.097 --> 08:39.644
Since that fateful day,
no soul's seeds have come to my garden.

08:41.145 --> 08:43.397
Except for one last foreign flower.

08:44.273 --> 08:45.858
Alive, as you can see.

08:58.037 --> 09:00.206
MAN FOUND DEAD AFTER TRAIL COLLAPSE
ON MOUNT CHEONGPUNG

09:00.289 --> 09:02.875
-A suicide? Murder?
-A man or woman?

09:02.959 --> 09:05.253
What on earth happened?
Are they even dead?

09:05.336 --> 09:06.379
Tell us!

09:06.462 --> 09:07.964
Stand back. Give them room!

09:11.300 --> 09:14.595
Hey, who the hell are you?
Why are you in front of my home?

09:15.388 --> 09:17.265
-Huh?
-Daddy?

09:18.432 --> 09:21.310
-I missed you! Look! I've come home!
-What the--

09:21.394 --> 09:22.812
-I'm a good boy!
-Oh, my God!

09:22.895 --> 09:24.730
You lunatic! Why are you jumping around?

09:24.814 --> 09:26.649
-Psycho!
-Yes, jump! I can jump!

09:26.732 --> 09:28.276
It's Ppoppi! I've come home!

09:28.901 --> 09:32.572
-See? I'm back! I'm so sorry, Daddy.
-What?

09:36.242 --> 09:38.160
Ha-neul! Ha-neul, it's me!

09:39.620 --> 09:42.748
Whoa! Who the hell are you?
How do you know my son's name?

09:43.958 --> 09:46.127
Hey, keep your hands off him, got it?

09:46.711 --> 09:48.754
It's me, your brother! See, Ha-neul?

09:49.297 --> 09:51.716
Daddy, it's me. It's Ppoppi.

09:54.885 --> 09:55.803
Oh, my face.

09:56.929 --> 09:58.180
Chauffeur Kim.

09:58.264 --> 09:59.974
I need another wish.

10:01.058 --> 10:04.353
I know. Let's go back to the village.
Immediately.

10:05.271 --> 10:06.105
Ppoppi, bang!

10:09.984 --> 10:10.818
Ppoppi, "V."

10:12.903 --> 10:15.364
-Ppoppi, nose.
-Hey, hey, hey, stop.

10:15.448 --> 10:19.493
Ppoppi, I missed you.

10:20.411 --> 10:22.455
Papa, my dog!

10:23.164 --> 10:26.000
Ppoppi, why are you a person?

10:26.083 --> 10:28.336
I wished for it.

10:29.086 --> 10:30.880
I have a secret I've been hiding.

10:32.632 --> 10:34.050
See, I made a wish--

10:34.133 --> 10:36.344
Get away from him, you lunatic!
I'll kill you!

10:37.136 --> 10:38.888
Son of a bitch.

10:42.767 --> 10:45.978
Ha-neul. Just wait a little while, okay?

10:47.647 --> 10:50.858
I'll come back, Daddy. Okay?
Okay. Good doggy!

10:51.567 --> 10:53.778
-Man's insane.
-Chauffeur Kim, start the car.

10:54.695 --> 10:56.280
-Let's go for a ride.
-We'll wait.

11:01.952 --> 11:03.287
ODD TEETH AND ODD PEOPLE WELCOME

11:03.371 --> 11:04.580
Wisdom teeth?

11:05.164 --> 11:07.375
Your gums are swollen,
we can't extract today.

11:08.709 --> 11:10.836
Let's get an X-ray
to see if they're impacted.

11:10.920 --> 11:12.004
All right.

11:12.088 --> 11:13.881
Go ahead and spit before we move on.

11:13.964 --> 11:17.885
Oh, my. How am I almost 80 years old
and still dealing with wisdom teeth?

11:18.969 --> 11:21.347
I won't be too long, will I?
The foodbank needs volunteers.

11:22.473 --> 11:23.307
Mmm?

11:33.943 --> 11:37.405
Oh, my. You're very efficient
for such a young lady.

11:37.488 --> 11:39.657
I've only made family dinners.

11:40.282 --> 11:43.828
Just happy that I can be useful again.

11:43.911 --> 11:45.454
Oh, my. Hello!

11:46.038 --> 11:47.373
Hello. Hello.

11:49.041 --> 11:52.086
This is our CEO, Ryu Su-hyeon.
His money funds the foodbank.

11:52.169 --> 11:54.922
This here is our newest volunteer,
Miss Lee Mi-ju.

11:55.005 --> 11:57.007
Pleased to see you again.

11:58.217 --> 11:59.844
I wanted to see that face of yours.

12:01.137 --> 12:03.597
What the… He wants to see my face?

12:04.140 --> 12:06.434
Don't tell me…

12:06.517 --> 12:10.396
Oh, Pan-geum, you little minx!

12:11.397 --> 12:13.816
Have we met? I don't believe we have.

12:14.608 --> 12:17.361
Indeed, we have. Hmm.

12:18.070 --> 12:20.948
Your kind, you crave beauty and youth.

12:21.907 --> 12:24.201
But don't expect for your lifespan
to be extended further.

12:24.285 --> 12:26.537
Though your body is young,
your age is still the same.

12:27.371 --> 12:28.247
How naive.

12:31.625 --> 12:32.668
My age?

12:34.378 --> 12:36.213
-Wait. Wait, hold on!
-Hey!

12:37.590 --> 12:41.510
Excuse me, Mr. Ryu!
What exactly did you mean by all of that?

12:46.056 --> 12:48.684
What did I mean by that?
You sure you want to know?

12:48.768 --> 12:52.271
You've already met a genie, now an angel.
You sure have been lucky, haven't you?

12:53.731 --> 12:54.899
I've met a…

12:56.192 --> 12:57.485
An… an angel?

13:03.407 --> 13:05.868
You have. The angel, Ejllael.

13:06.827 --> 13:08.370
I am also the harbinger of death.

13:09.830 --> 13:11.707
The harbinger?

13:12.249 --> 13:13.751
Arrogant human.

13:14.585 --> 13:16.045
Volunteering at a foodbank.

13:16.128 --> 13:18.923
You thought such a pathetic act
would alleviate your secret?

13:19.006 --> 13:21.550
Did you think your younger body
would give you a longer life?

13:21.634 --> 13:23.177
How completely absurd.

13:24.428 --> 13:25.721
I… I don't understand.

13:26.514 --> 13:27.348
Explain yourself!

13:27.431 --> 13:31.060
It means that though you seem young,
your lifespan is still unchanged. Mortal.

13:31.811 --> 13:34.855
Since you have done a fine job
raising your granddaughter,

13:34.939 --> 13:36.649
you'll be granted passage into heaven.

13:44.240 --> 13:45.282
Listen.

13:46.700 --> 13:49.036
When the flowers next bloom
in your front yard,

13:51.080 --> 13:52.039
you will die.

14:02.466 --> 14:03.801
We are so very ashamed.

14:05.970 --> 14:08.722
The full amount that was transferred out
due to a processing issue

14:08.806 --> 14:11.183
has been reimbursed
to your account, Miss Ki Ka-young.

14:14.937 --> 14:15.813
Fine.

14:16.814 --> 14:19.733
I fell off a cliff recently,
so I'm a little out of sorts.

14:19.817 --> 14:20.860
I'm going to go now.

14:23.988 --> 14:25.489
-Uh…
-Oh, what?

14:25.573 --> 14:26.866
Is there an issue?

14:27.449 --> 14:28.993
Is the amount of money wrong?

14:29.076 --> 14:30.119
The amount is fine.

14:31.954 --> 14:35.916
Although, I think
I'll take the balance in cash.

14:36.000 --> 14:39.128
In cash? The entire balance? What?

14:40.588 --> 14:42.631
You see, with such a large amount,

14:42.715 --> 14:44.884
you must disclose the reason
for withdrawal.

14:45.676 --> 14:47.887
It's such a large amount, you understand.

14:48.762 --> 14:53.017
Many often just say it's for their wedding
and just leave it at that.

14:53.100 --> 14:56.186
Yes. I suppose it's all for my wedding.

14:57.396 --> 14:59.690
Every last cent. It's all mine.

15:00.733 --> 15:02.192
You bastard, psycho bitch!

15:02.943 --> 15:04.028
Have you gone insane?

15:13.120 --> 15:13.954
Hmm.

15:16.165 --> 15:17.207
Those bastards.

15:20.920 --> 15:21.754
Hmm.

15:51.742 --> 15:53.410
I heard you had an accident on the cliff.

15:53.953 --> 15:55.829
I wanted to see
if you were all right, sweetie.

15:56.413 --> 15:59.875
"Sweetie"? That makes this a little weird.

15:59.959 --> 16:01.585
Your father and I were fellow students.

16:02.294 --> 16:04.463
Wait, is it not weird anymore?
Since he's dead?

16:05.464 --> 16:06.632
You are indeed smart.

16:07.549 --> 16:08.467
You know who I am.

16:10.803 --> 16:11.637
I have an inkling.

16:13.722 --> 16:14.682
Is it you?

16:15.474 --> 16:17.476
Are you the same boy
I saved centuries ago?

16:18.811 --> 16:20.187
Not that smart, I see.

16:21.480 --> 16:24.233
It's Shaytan! It's the wrath of Iblis!

16:24.733 --> 16:26.068
It's the wrath of Iblis!

16:26.735 --> 16:28.112
Khalid. Khalid!

16:30.698 --> 16:31.699
Khalid!

16:35.828 --> 16:37.162
What have you done, Khalid?

16:38.831 --> 16:40.249
You were only half-right.

16:40.833 --> 16:42.543
You did start it,
so you should end it too.

16:43.877 --> 16:46.797
Where is the lamp?
You have one wish remaining.

16:47.798 --> 16:50.384
And it would please me greatly
if you made that wish.

16:50.467 --> 16:53.679
I'd like to terminate
my tedious immortality.

17:03.105 --> 17:05.566
I can see through your lies. You punk.

17:10.279 --> 17:11.155
You've got my back?

17:32.176 --> 17:33.469
It heals right away.

17:34.720 --> 17:36.555
I could open your throat
and you wouldn't die.

17:37.139 --> 17:38.307
I'm afraid not.

17:38.390 --> 17:41.351
I've got you! I've got you! I got you!

17:41.435 --> 17:42.519
What the--

17:42.603 --> 17:45.105
-It's a jaguar! A jaguar!
-Oh!

17:45.189 --> 17:47.941
I've known this jaguar
since the 11th century.

17:48.025 --> 17:49.151
They're the dangerous ones.

17:49.735 --> 17:52.154
Yes! Yes, we know. We've seen them around.

17:53.238 --> 17:55.449
Hey, hey. Do you remember me?

17:56.033 --> 17:57.910
You get to decide.
Will you be captured alive

17:57.993 --> 17:59.661
or be captured stone dead?

17:59.745 --> 18:01.830
But no matter what, you will be caught.

18:02.539 --> 18:04.750
Korean men have an obligation
to our national defense.

18:04.833 --> 18:07.628
-So we're basically killers. And we are--
-Retreat.

18:16.220 --> 18:17.888
Ha! See that?

18:18.472 --> 18:20.974
Look at those chickens!
Yeah, run away. Chickens.

18:21.892 --> 18:23.393
You all right?

18:24.019 --> 18:26.188
They really seemed sketchy,
so we decided to tail them,

18:26.271 --> 18:28.148
and those bastards
were following you around.

18:28.232 --> 18:31.360
But what's really weird is that
one of them vanishes every day.

18:31.902 --> 18:34.905
I'm saying that one of them dies
every day, over and over.

18:37.449 --> 18:38.826
-Chang-sik.
-Huh?

18:38.909 --> 18:40.494
-May I ask you a favor?
-Uh-huh.

18:40.577 --> 18:42.371
I know this is all very weird.

18:42.454 --> 18:44.957
I'm afraid you have all entered
a very weird world.

18:45.624 --> 18:48.127
Uh, a world with jaguars like this one.

18:48.210 --> 18:50.337
Oh!

18:52.256 --> 18:53.298
Don't worry about me.

18:53.882 --> 18:56.718
I'd appreciate it if you could take care
of Mi-ju and Min-ji.

18:57.302 --> 18:58.220
I assume that…

18:58.762 --> 19:01.640
these two cannot know
of this dangerous situation.

19:01.723 --> 19:03.767
They must not be left vulnerable
to attack, right?

19:03.851 --> 19:05.644
-Yes, spot on.
-Don't worry, Miss Ki.

19:05.727 --> 19:06.770
Yes.

19:06.854 --> 19:10.357
Seeing this guy in person,
I can see he's not so scary.

19:10.440 --> 19:11.984
He's a kitty. Big kitty.

19:12.651 --> 19:14.778
I'm glad we could clear the air.

19:14.862 --> 19:16.822
Get him away! Back off, panther!

19:30.752 --> 19:32.462
Long time no see, brother.

19:33.505 --> 19:35.340
You came to me at my worst.

19:35.424 --> 19:39.428
Yes. It's truly been a while.
Wouldn't you say, brother?

19:41.638 --> 19:43.182
Should I be concerned?

19:43.265 --> 19:46.185
Does your presence here
mean my son is in danger?

19:48.061 --> 19:48.896
He might be.

19:50.272 --> 19:52.858
How the wishes of your master enraged me.

19:54.401 --> 19:57.487
And your reckless decision
to create this eternal body.

19:57.571 --> 19:58.405
Khalid!

19:58.488 --> 20:01.408
How I regret putting my son's soul
into that body.

20:03.660 --> 20:04.494
Yes.

20:05.329 --> 20:08.040
My hubris caused me
to make a wrong decision.

20:08.874 --> 20:12.044
That's why I've come here now
to give you a chance.

20:12.628 --> 20:16.965
But that immortal, he cannot be the one
to decide her final wish.

20:18.634 --> 20:21.803
That boy may try to threaten her,
as menacingly as he can.

20:22.471 --> 20:24.014
She has the final say over it.

20:24.097 --> 20:28.227
I'm determined that her last wish
will be a righteous one.

20:28.810 --> 20:32.272
You believe that strongly in your
friend? If you're right, you'll be killed.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.025
That's no longer my concern.

20:35.817 --> 20:38.987
I've already decided to let Him
send me to Hell once and for all.

20:40.405 --> 20:43.325
And if you wish to protect your son
from danger,

20:43.951 --> 20:46.411
you will see to it he doesn't make
the wrong decision either.

20:47.162 --> 20:49.998
And if your son
does make the wrong decision,

20:50.999 --> 20:52.459
if the lamp should be his,

20:53.585 --> 20:54.836
I will end his life.

21:01.009 --> 21:04.137
I cannot restrain my son for too long.

21:05.055 --> 21:07.683
That could harm those
who are innocent in this matter.

21:09.977 --> 21:11.853
He is a being even worse than me.

21:13.480 --> 21:15.190
An actual, real shaytan.

21:16.525 --> 21:19.569
I will try to hinder my son
for as long as possible.

21:21.029 --> 21:22.906
That is all I can promise.

21:25.325 --> 21:27.119
If that's to be the case,

21:27.202 --> 21:31.081
I'm afraid your son's fate
is still precarious, brother.

21:32.249 --> 21:33.834
I am not merciful.

21:33.917 --> 21:37.796
I will show him none,
even if he is your son.

21:52.227 --> 21:56.523
CLOSED TEMPORARILY
DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS

21:57.899 --> 22:00.694
-Right. That's her.
-That's her there?

22:00.777 --> 22:03.488
I saw her walk out of the bank
with a ton of cash today.

22:04.072 --> 22:06.158
Careful. They say she's a psychopath.

22:06.241 --> 22:07.367
Oh. Is that so?

22:07.868 --> 22:09.453
That means she's rich!

22:09.536 --> 22:11.413
-Those Wall Street bankers are psycho.
-Yeah!

22:11.496 --> 22:13.123
Regular people like us

22:13.206 --> 22:15.000
aren't as successful as psychos like her.

22:16.418 --> 22:17.544
You bitch!

22:19.504 --> 22:20.714
Fuck you.

22:23.008 --> 22:24.217
All right now.

22:25.052 --> 22:26.928
There's an easy solution to all this.

22:27.679 --> 22:30.223
Psycho sweetie, hand over the money,
am I clear?

22:31.850 --> 22:32.684
Huh?

22:49.659 --> 22:51.953
Who is that? Whoa.

22:52.788 --> 22:54.831
Were those stairs always there?

22:55.916 --> 22:58.502
Uh, I'm pretty sure
they weren't there before.

23:03.340 --> 23:05.967
I left Sade with you,
so why did you call me?

23:07.719 --> 23:10.055
He just popped out to relieve himself.

23:10.847 --> 23:12.682
I was just punched in the face.

23:12.766 --> 23:13.975
Beat them up!

23:15.268 --> 23:17.312
They punched you in the face? Wow.

23:18.772 --> 23:20.524
Well, that's something I can't tolerate.

23:26.655 --> 23:28.115
-What's going on?
-Who are you?

23:28.198 --> 23:31.076
What's happening?

23:39.876 --> 23:40.710
Don't wait up.

23:48.760 --> 23:50.720
Hey, hey. You're not supposed to be here!

23:57.477 --> 24:01.398
What is this?
I swear, I'll be good from now on.

24:01.481 --> 24:03.442
-Someone help me!
-Where am I?

24:04.526 --> 24:06.153
How do I get out of here? Help!

24:06.236 --> 24:09.072
I swear! I promise to change! Please!

24:09.156 --> 24:10.323
What's this place?

24:11.283 --> 24:12.117
Where are we?

24:12.200 --> 24:14.619
This is where I landed
when I was kicked out of heaven.

24:16.121 --> 24:17.080
The Underworld.

24:19.207 --> 24:20.208
This is where you were?

24:21.751 --> 24:22.752
For how long?

24:24.629 --> 24:25.505
I'm not sure.

24:26.298 --> 24:31.261
But I suppose you humans
would call it "eternity."

24:33.013 --> 24:36.433
Even with this fate, you still wouldn't
bow your head to humans?

24:37.726 --> 24:38.602
That bad?

24:40.312 --> 24:41.146
That was the case.

24:44.483 --> 24:47.444
Just to be sure,
you'll take me out of here, right?

24:47.527 --> 24:49.446
You haven't treated me as a human
all that much.

24:51.072 --> 24:52.532
I would just like to be sure.

24:52.616 --> 24:55.702
Remember how you wouldn't spot me any cash
when I asked?

24:55.785 --> 24:58.038
And dinner?
You'd get annoyed when I asked.

24:58.121 --> 25:00.999
And the black string?
Instead of breaking it off my wrist,

25:01.082 --> 25:02.667
you ran to the shed to get the giant--

25:03.710 --> 25:07.297
I'm treating you with care.
Oh, my dear Genie is warm.

25:07.964 --> 25:09.549
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

25:10.342 --> 25:11.968
I do not consent.

25:12.636 --> 25:13.470
Hmm.

25:15.472 --> 25:17.265
I guess for us…

25:19.184 --> 25:21.186
it always ends this way. Let's go.

25:23.855 --> 25:24.773
Come on.

25:31.530 --> 25:33.782
Where have you been?
I told you to rush over.

25:33.865 --> 25:37.786
I'm sorry, but where does one find
a velvet coat hanger at this hour?

25:37.869 --> 25:39.496
Luckily, Irem had one.

25:39.579 --> 25:43.416
From now on, you and I
must be on the same page.

25:44.251 --> 25:45.085
Now,

25:45.669 --> 25:48.463
very carefully pull it over the top
to the bottom.

25:49.130 --> 25:51.091
We can't let any dust
fall off of this coat.

25:51.675 --> 25:54.344
All its molecules, filth, air, atoms,
brightness, saturation,

25:54.427 --> 25:57.430
every piece of evidence of Hell.
Every souvenir.

25:57.514 --> 25:59.182
Dust from Hell?

26:02.811 --> 26:06.523
Gosh, you're in an awfully good mood
for someone just back from Hell.

26:06.606 --> 26:09.776
I dodged every hit today. Not one landed.

26:10.318 --> 26:13.863
I think I've clocked your pattern
of attack. It's right, left, left, center.

26:13.947 --> 26:15.907
Easy.

26:15.991 --> 26:17.158
Not exactly.

26:18.159 --> 26:19.202
Go hang this over there.

26:22.455 --> 26:25.792
The immortal being was that kid.
My classmate's son.

26:27.127 --> 26:28.795
He brought his car into the garage.

26:30.171 --> 26:32.340
You're kind of right, but only half-right.

26:34.009 --> 26:37.012
He said that too.
I'm only ever half-right, I guess.

26:37.679 --> 26:39.264
Pray tell me what I've gotten so wrong?

26:40.515 --> 26:43.268
Shadi swapped his son's soul
with the immortal being's.

26:44.394 --> 26:48.231
The boy you hoped would live a long life
was unable to do so.

26:49.941 --> 26:51.401
The immortal one…

26:53.028 --> 26:53.945
is Khalid.

26:55.238 --> 26:56.573
Khalid.

26:57.449 --> 26:58.950
The one in the hourglass?

27:00.076 --> 27:03.955
That ingrate. I was so nice to him,
and this is how he treats me?

27:04.539 --> 27:06.916
Mr. Genie! Mr. Genie!

27:08.168 --> 27:09.002
Mr. Genie.

27:10.503 --> 27:12.797
I found my dad! I found my home!

27:12.881 --> 27:15.884
I saw my brother, Ha-neul too.

27:15.967 --> 27:18.470
Are you… Kim Gae?

27:20.221 --> 27:23.642
Oh. Has anyone told you
you look so much like Daniel Henney?

27:25.101 --> 27:27.228
Hey. Bad dog.

27:28.146 --> 27:29.648
Oh. Sorry.

27:30.690 --> 27:31.524
Habit.

27:32.776 --> 27:33.985
Mr. Genie.

27:34.069 --> 27:38.448
I'd like to return to being a dog. Please.

27:43.912 --> 27:45.580
Sir!

27:45.664 --> 27:46.498
What's wrong?

27:47.791 --> 27:50.585
Oh, no. Mr. Kim, are you sick?
We need to get you to a hospital.

27:50.669 --> 27:53.004
No. No. No.

27:53.588 --> 27:56.466
Every time I go see the doctor,
they get mad.

27:57.008 --> 27:59.302
"We can't afford this dog's surgery."

27:59.386 --> 28:00.553
See, my dad gets angry.

28:00.637 --> 28:04.224
"Ppoppi, bad boy. Bad boy!"

28:04.891 --> 28:06.935
Let me clean the blood.

28:08.478 --> 28:11.773
Hang on, sir, I'm confused.
Why do you say you're a dog?

28:11.856 --> 28:15.485
You can't think like that.
I've known assholes who are absolute dogs.

28:17.320 --> 28:19.406
Sir, believe me, you're a good person.

28:19.989 --> 28:20.865
Chauffeur Kim.

28:21.616 --> 28:23.910
Thank you. I leave all my money to you.

28:24.494 --> 28:26.371
It's all yours. All of it.

28:27.205 --> 28:28.081
I'm done with it.

28:29.457 --> 28:31.376
Mr. Genie, please do it.

28:31.459 --> 28:33.253
You want this to be your final wish?

28:34.838 --> 28:36.756
Wait. Look, before that,
ask your family first.

28:37.340 --> 28:39.843
Ask if they lost a dog,
if they're looking for one.

28:42.053 --> 28:42.887
If they miss it.

28:43.471 --> 28:46.141
No, it's… it's too late now.

28:47.392 --> 28:50.270
I need to tell Ha-neul goodbye.

28:50.854 --> 28:53.064
-Don't say that.
-So I have to go.

28:54.107 --> 28:56.693
This is my final wish.

28:59.821 --> 29:01.322
How'd we get here?

29:15.754 --> 29:16.921
It's been fulfilled.

29:57.670 --> 29:59.923
She got to the bus terminal,
but never got on one.

30:00.006 --> 30:01.925
Then she went back out to catch a taxi.

30:03.968 --> 30:04.844
Why?

30:07.305 --> 30:08.932
If that kid is Khalid,

30:09.015 --> 30:11.976
can't you just go back in time
and see what happened back then?

30:12.727 --> 30:13.770
Believe me, I tried.

30:14.521 --> 30:16.981
Thing is, I can't travel
back to that time.

30:17.565 --> 30:19.734
-Why?
-He is blocking me.

30:20.485 --> 30:23.446
He has given me three wishes as well.

30:25.240 --> 30:26.449
Wow, you get around.

30:28.243 --> 30:29.994
And then? Tell me what you wished for.

30:30.078 --> 30:35.375
Well, my first wish was the ability to
offer wishes to send His creation to Hell.

30:36.251 --> 30:39.295
My second wish was
to no longer be contained,

30:39.379 --> 30:41.464
so that I might corrupt a new master.

30:42.340 --> 30:44.050
That means you've got one final wish left.

30:46.261 --> 30:47.512
I thought so too.

30:51.057 --> 30:51.891
See…

30:54.435 --> 30:56.020
I think the third wish

30:57.564 --> 30:59.190
has been granted to me already.

31:03.361 --> 31:04.696
I have another question.

31:05.697 --> 31:08.700
Do you bear witness
that she saw someone else,

31:08.783 --> 31:12.704
another foreigner,
accompanying you in 1041?

31:13.955 --> 31:14.956
Yes, I'll bear witness.

31:18.877 --> 31:21.588
She was from the East. She was beautiful.

31:22.463 --> 31:24.591
At first, she was weak and wilted,

31:25.466 --> 31:26.718
and about to fall.

31:27.719 --> 31:29.888
However, she managed to endure,

31:29.971 --> 31:32.557
surviving for 28 years in total.

31:34.851 --> 31:36.895
Not just a mere eight years?

31:36.978 --> 31:37.979
No.

31:39.063 --> 31:40.982
She persisted for another 20.

31:44.027 --> 31:46.988
During all of your lost years,
the immortal flower lived.

31:52.493 --> 31:54.454
I can't remember what my wish was for.

31:58.416 --> 31:59.417
But I think…

32:03.171 --> 32:04.631
it resulted in a bad ending.

32:11.262 --> 32:12.430
So I'm scared.

32:17.060 --> 32:18.978
When I was falling, I was scared too.

32:20.396 --> 32:23.524
Scared about who I'd never see again.
Grandma and Min-ji.

32:26.277 --> 32:29.739
And you. The thought of never seeing
any of you again,

32:31.449 --> 32:34.285
it just made me feel so angry.
That's fear, isn't it?

32:36.537 --> 32:37.538
It's pretty close.

32:39.415 --> 32:43.127
Guess I've climbed high in the ranks.
I even beat your garage and frogs too.

32:44.504 --> 32:47.382
You only just squeaked past the frogs.

32:52.887 --> 32:55.640
Do you have your own place like I do?

32:57.642 --> 32:59.769
A rooftop where it's high and quiet?

33:01.145 --> 33:01.980
Where you can think?

33:08.403 --> 33:10.029
This is last spring.

33:11.614 --> 33:13.074
This is your safe place?

33:14.867 --> 33:18.329
When do the bats, snakes and cockroaches
all come out?

33:18.413 --> 33:20.164
Stop that. I get squeamish.

33:21.749 --> 33:23.710
Earwig, woodlice.

33:23.793 --> 33:25.211
Stop, knock it off.

33:26.295 --> 33:28.297
Didn't we come here for me to relax?

33:29.674 --> 33:32.677
That's too bad.
I know a ton of disgusting things.

33:34.762 --> 33:35.763
Why do you like it here?

33:36.848 --> 33:38.474
It's…

33:39.225 --> 33:40.226
so beautiful.

33:43.062 --> 33:44.522
I've lived so long,

33:46.357 --> 33:47.734
but I've never seen this.

33:51.696 --> 33:54.157
It seemed like a nice idea
to return to this time.

33:54.240 --> 33:55.575
This was…

33:56.909 --> 33:58.453
This was not that long ago.

33:59.579 --> 34:01.873
You were trying your hardest
to get revenge,

34:02.790 --> 34:03.624
weren't you?

34:06.586 --> 34:09.088
I decided after this to hold off

34:10.339 --> 34:11.340
on corrupting you.

34:15.386 --> 34:18.639
If I had really wanted revenge,
you would already be dead.

34:35.073 --> 34:36.449
So this is when it started.

34:37.950 --> 34:39.035
When the flowers withered.

34:41.120 --> 34:43.122
You no longer like the idea of me dying.

34:53.341 --> 34:55.301
And here I was, thinking I was first.

35:08.272 --> 35:09.148
It is pretty.

35:31.671 --> 35:34.966
Is this true? Ka-young was confronted
by the immortal one?

35:35.716 --> 35:38.344
YES. HE WENT PERSONALLY
TO THE AUTO SHOP

35:40.721 --> 35:41.931
That stupid idiot!

35:42.932 --> 35:45.977
I overlooked the determination of humans.

35:47.895 --> 35:51.315
Hang on. If he's going to carry about
like this, I should be using him.

35:52.191 --> 35:53.693
Is the lamp the best path here?

35:55.486 --> 35:59.574
COULD YOU PLEASE REPEAT THAT FOR ME?
I COULDN'T READ YOUR LIPS

35:59.657 --> 36:00.908
Okay, look.

36:05.872 --> 36:07.456
-Have you learned your lesson?
-Mmm!

36:07.540 --> 36:09.083
-Not going to do that again?
-Mmm-mmm!

36:24.807 --> 36:28.311
Listen. When the flowers next bloom
in your front yard,

36:29.061 --> 36:30.021
you will die.

36:39.363 --> 36:40.781
Where in the world is she?

36:41.532 --> 36:42.950
-Miss Yoo?
-Yes?

36:43.034 --> 36:46.871
Could you pull up Lee Mi-ju…
Uh, Ki Ka-young's X-ray for me?

36:46.954 --> 36:48.497
Sure.

36:49.290 --> 36:51.417
While on the subject,
why is Lee Mi-ju

36:51.500 --> 36:52.710
filed under Miss Ki Ka-young?

36:53.586 --> 36:55.338
Because I decided to, that's why.

36:56.214 --> 36:57.048
Right.

36:57.757 --> 36:58.966
I've sent you her X-ray.

37:02.220 --> 37:03.512
KI KA-YOUNG

37:04.931 --> 37:06.682
Huh?

37:08.976 --> 37:11.062
OH PAN-GEUM

37:15.524 --> 37:17.401
KI KA-YOUNG
OH PAN-GEUM

37:19.987 --> 37:22.865
OH PAN-GEUM

37:24.784 --> 37:27.620
KI KA-YOUNG
OH PAN-GEUM

37:33.376 --> 37:35.586
Get 20 pounds of sun-dried salt.

37:35.670 --> 37:37.463
I'm going to separate the doenjang.

37:47.848 --> 37:49.183
What brings you here?

37:49.267 --> 37:50.977
Ah. It's you, Ka-young.

37:52.103 --> 37:53.729
You see those cashiers?

37:57.858 --> 37:58.693
The cashiers?

37:58.776 --> 38:02.280
Ka-young, you've always been
a bit unusual,

38:02.363 --> 38:04.282
so I feel you'll understand.

38:05.866 --> 38:09.370
It's about, uh…
Well, it's my daughter-in-law.

38:09.453 --> 38:11.580
Although she's not anymore
since the divorce.

38:12.206 --> 38:15.167
They say she's been so upset
after they let her go as manager

38:15.251 --> 38:16.502
that now she just drinks.

38:18.129 --> 38:19.422
I see it otherwise.

38:20.298 --> 38:21.841
She has always been so exhausted.

38:22.800 --> 38:24.969
She was someone who saw
face cream as a splurge.

38:25.553 --> 38:26.887
She used to stand over there.

38:30.349 --> 38:31.350
Hi, Mother.

38:32.018 --> 38:33.060
Hi, Mother!

38:33.644 --> 38:34.729
"Hi, Mother."

38:35.563 --> 38:37.481
There was once a time when she did that.

38:39.442 --> 38:40.735
I have no clue what this is.

38:42.570 --> 38:44.196
Maybe it's dementia.

38:47.867 --> 38:49.785
You spirits, or angels or whatever,

38:50.536 --> 38:52.163
you all act so high and mighty.

38:52.705 --> 38:54.123
But look at Grandma An.

38:54.665 --> 38:57.793
Grandma An,
still desperately grasping onto

38:57.877 --> 38:59.920
a whole life that you just evaporated.

39:03.049 --> 39:04.925
It doesn't actually improve anything.

39:05.801 --> 39:07.511
It only makes the suffering worse.

39:09.930 --> 39:10.890
Well…

39:12.850 --> 39:14.518
I guess we're all just bound to suffer.

39:22.818 --> 39:26.238
By the way, why is the lamp
covered in graffiti around the inside?

39:26.322 --> 39:27.448
They all swear words?

39:28.199 --> 39:30.284
Swear words? Graffiti?

39:31.994 --> 39:33.662
I don't know what you're talking about.

39:37.291 --> 39:39.752
So, what are you saying is in here?

39:41.379 --> 39:42.463
Are you kidding?

39:43.172 --> 39:45.591
There's Arabic everywhere
all over every surface.

39:46.092 --> 39:47.968
It's all over the floors, the walls.

39:48.719 --> 39:51.222
-Huh?
-You really don't see it?

39:51.972 --> 39:53.015
Whatever. Move.

40:28.467 --> 40:31.512
So you mean, this is all written
in my lamp right now?

40:33.973 --> 40:35.224
Over there. See?

40:35.766 --> 40:37.768
You said you speak Arabic. What's it say?

40:41.439 --> 40:44.191
"You, who came from Goryeo, are enslaved."

40:45.109 --> 40:47.361
-"Serves you right."
-You believe it now?

40:49.196 --> 40:51.782
So mean. You got a death wish?

40:52.324 --> 40:53.409
Oh.

40:54.160 --> 40:55.828
Here. What does this one say?

40:59.415 --> 41:03.794
"You never make any money and yet
you keep selling your scrawny dates."

41:05.337 --> 41:07.715
How lovely. So romantic.

41:08.757 --> 41:11.051
There. That one. You're dead, by the way.

41:20.853 --> 41:24.064
"You wish upon stars.
I tell you I'm a genie."

41:28.569 --> 41:33.032
"No matter how often I remind you,
you spend your wishes on silly stars."

41:33.115 --> 41:35.618
"But all your wishes
are for me to be well."

41:37.244 --> 41:40.247
"You clearly think so lowly of me."

41:45.503 --> 41:46.670
This message…

41:49.256 --> 41:52.760
Our history. Our memories.
That's what I think it is.

41:55.054 --> 41:56.722
A sliver of our lost years.

42:02.436 --> 42:06.065
All right. It appears we've forgotten
our past together,

42:06.148 --> 42:08.192
around 20 years.
Who wants to help find it?

42:09.318 --> 42:10.486
I don't have any idea.

42:11.070 --> 42:12.655
I don't have Master's approval.

42:13.447 --> 42:15.574
I don't want to help you.

42:17.243 --> 42:20.579
Fine. Will you or will you not tell me
what Ejllael is hiding from me?

42:20.663 --> 42:23.624
-I don't have any idea.
-I don't want to help you.

42:28.504 --> 42:29.380
Irem.

42:31.423 --> 42:32.258
A moment.

42:39.181 --> 42:41.433
Irem! Ah!

42:42.726 --> 42:45.187
Wow, she's tough.

42:45.980 --> 42:49.400
Have you ever seen us two at any point
in the last couple 1,000 years?

42:49.483 --> 42:51.485
I mean, just blink once to mean, "yes."

42:52.528 --> 42:53.529
Just a moment.

42:56.282 --> 42:58.075
Master, aren't you being harsh?

42:58.659 --> 43:00.035
Your love shouldn't be allowed

43:00.119 --> 43:01.829
-to cause pain to my love.
-Um, okay.

43:01.912 --> 43:04.498
Irem!

43:05.165 --> 43:07.543
Open your socket wide,
we need to put this back in.

43:08.377 --> 43:10.254
-I'll just toss a soft ball.
-Hold on.

43:10.337 --> 43:13.591
Did this Genie kiss Jinniya,
or did he not?

43:14.174 --> 43:16.594
Was his mouth in the right spot to do so?

43:16.677 --> 43:18.846
-That, I can answer.
-Irem is out due to her injuries.

43:19.513 --> 43:21.807
You and I, one-on-one. Him on the line.

43:24.935 --> 43:25.853
I have things to do.

43:30.274 --> 43:33.277
Mmm. So you both pretend
to be busy as an excuse.

43:33.360 --> 43:34.737
Wait!

43:35.946 --> 43:39.033
Irem! Watch out for your wings!

43:39.116 --> 43:41.035
You're a national treasure!

43:43.996 --> 43:45.664
Irem!

43:48.167 --> 43:50.878
We did learn that we've forgotten
our history together.

43:51.462 --> 43:52.838
That's a win.

43:54.465 --> 43:57.551
I learned you kissed Jinniya.
I wouldn't call that a win.

44:00.179 --> 44:01.305
I didn't say that.

44:07.102 --> 44:07.936
Eom Sang-tae.

44:11.732 --> 44:13.484
Will he really go to the past?

44:13.567 --> 44:16.403
Even if he does, you won't know
any of the circumstances.

44:17.946 --> 44:19.448
Sure you want to take part in this?

44:20.699 --> 44:21.700
Absolutely.

44:23.744 --> 44:27.373
Hmm. Although I should bring
the wooden bat I keep next to the closet.

44:27.456 --> 44:31.168
I already know. I'm definitely
going to try to save the girl.

44:31.960 --> 44:34.880
-This wish is important.
-I know. I'll lose again.

44:35.881 --> 44:38.509
And I'm fated to die if I lose,
since it's tied to my first wish.

44:38.592 --> 44:42.221
But I'll still do it. I can be selfless,
even though I was born evil.

44:42.304 --> 44:44.264
Despite that, I can still do a good deed.

44:46.892 --> 44:50.813
Besides, if we're meant to die,
let's make it a fun death.

44:52.481 --> 44:54.316
Protect me as you always do.

44:54.983 --> 44:56.860
If I should die,
then I should die for you.

44:57.778 --> 45:01.365
And if you are meant to die, die for me.

45:05.452 --> 45:08.163
Okay. I can do that.

45:10.124 --> 45:10.999
Let's do that.

45:18.132 --> 45:19.967
You want to go back
to before you killed her?

45:20.050 --> 45:21.218
Isn't it obvious?

45:21.301 --> 45:24.888
To get to experience that thrill again?
Why would I waste that chance?

45:25.514 --> 45:28.934
But this time, I won't hit her
against my taillight or dye her hair.

45:29.768 --> 45:33.480
They'll never link it to the case
20 years ago.

45:35.816 --> 45:36.942
This time around,

45:38.318 --> 45:41.321
I'll just chop her up
into little teeny bits.

45:41.405 --> 45:43.782
Ah. That's your plan?

45:45.659 --> 45:48.412
I should rework my approach
if that's how it is.

45:48.495 --> 45:50.497
Do it! Put the effort in!

45:50.581 --> 45:52.040
You're my genie, aren't you?

45:52.875 --> 45:56.086
At night this time, p.m. 10 after 9:00.

45:56.670 --> 45:58.881
April 10th. You better make it p.m.!

45:59.548 --> 46:01.383
In front of
the Gangma Waterfall sign. Got it?

46:01.467 --> 46:02.509
GANGMA FALLS, 500M

46:04.553 --> 46:05.429
Absolutely.

46:07.014 --> 46:08.140
It's been fulfilled.

46:10.934 --> 46:12.478
What were your test scores?

46:12.561 --> 46:14.855
APRIL 10, 2024

46:16.023 --> 46:16.857
Phew.

46:18.108 --> 46:20.778
-Your grandma is really angry.
-Why?

46:21.361 --> 46:22.196
It was about…

46:23.405 --> 46:25.783
you achieving so much.
Just don't do it again.

46:28.494 --> 46:30.370
Also, I've arrived from your future.

46:31.246 --> 46:33.332
You were dug out of a sand dune. Get lost.

46:34.583 --> 46:35.459
It's true.

46:36.043 --> 46:38.962
This is what your future self
asked me to give you.

46:40.589 --> 46:41.882
Mmm?

46:47.054 --> 46:49.598
WRITTEN BY KI KA-YOUNG
A NEGATIVE ONE AND A STONE…

46:59.358 --> 47:01.443
EOM SANG-TAE IS THE MURDERER
HE WILL KILL AGAIN

47:01.527 --> 47:04.446
20-YEAR-OLD CORPSE
FOUND IN CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE

47:08.158 --> 47:11.328
HIS SIGNATURE SEEMS TO BE
DYEING HIS VICTIMS' HAIR BLACK

47:11.411 --> 47:14.581
SHE WILL GO MISSING TONIGHT
(APRIL 10, 2024) AROUND 9 P.M.

47:18.043 --> 47:20.546
I knew that asshole
would do something like that.

47:24.299 --> 47:25.259
You were right.

47:26.760 --> 47:27.594
You'll be too late.

47:31.056 --> 47:32.224
Hold on to me.

47:52.202 --> 47:54.246
Hmm? Hmm?

47:58.417 --> 48:00.252
I've definitely been here before.

48:05.340 --> 48:06.717
April. Right.

48:08.010 --> 48:08.844
Mr. Eom.

48:13.599 --> 48:15.100
Huh? What?

48:16.143 --> 48:17.477
I remember now.

48:18.437 --> 48:19.438
I'm so sorry.

48:20.439 --> 48:22.941
My phone. I wasn't paying attention
when I left.

48:23.734 --> 48:24.568
Your phone?

48:32.868 --> 48:35.495
I had it all wrong.

48:37.414 --> 48:39.333
Yeah, that's right, your phone.

48:40.375 --> 48:41.752
-It's over here. This way.
-Great.

48:43.921 --> 48:44.755
You know…

48:48.258 --> 48:51.386
I'm afraid I don't think
it's the right color, your hair.

48:52.304 --> 48:53.639
What?

49:07.277 --> 49:09.071
Where are you going?

49:09.154 --> 49:10.697
Get over here, you fucking bitch!

49:18.288 --> 49:20.040
-Fuck.
-Oh, yikes.

49:20.123 --> 49:22.542
He bought a chainsaw for this occasion.

49:22.626 --> 49:25.379
I made sure to only send his soul back
to this night.

49:25.462 --> 49:28.131
Miss… Miss Ki.

49:28.215 --> 49:30.592
What are you doing?

49:31.385 --> 49:33.720
-It's not what it looks like.
-Oh, no?

49:34.888 --> 49:36.348
Ooh!

49:36.431 --> 49:38.517
Don't you dare talk, you serial killer.

49:39.935 --> 49:40.894
Blood.

49:42.145 --> 49:44.439
You bitch! Why are you doing this?

49:44.523 --> 49:46.274
-Oh, no, he didn't.
-Just you wait.

49:46.775 --> 49:49.778
-I'll kill you next.
-Oh, shut up. You can't stop me.

49:51.571 --> 49:53.407
This is far too much fun!

49:54.866 --> 49:57.411
Ooh! Ooh!

49:57.995 --> 50:00.247
Yikes. Oh, gosh. Not his heel!

50:00.330 --> 50:03.166
Sir! Sir! Wait.
We need to call the police.

50:03.750 --> 50:05.752
-Oh, God. Oh, no.
-They're coming already.

50:06.545 --> 50:08.755
We go way back, you know. Oh!

50:13.969 --> 50:16.179
Oh, that was a good one.

50:26.273 --> 50:27.399
He tried to kill that woman.

50:27.983 --> 50:30.193
He smashed her head
right against this taillight here.

50:30.736 --> 50:32.195
You can see her hair stuck in it.

50:32.279 --> 50:35.157
-Oh.
-And this woman here took her bat and…

50:36.742 --> 50:37.909
Let's skip that part.

50:38.702 --> 50:42.831
I have a feeling a YouTuber will uncover
a 20-year-old skeleton soon.

50:42.914 --> 50:45.208
So I recommend you go through
that guy's house.

50:45.292 --> 50:47.711
Especially, his cellar. Mmm-hmm.

50:48.295 --> 50:53.008
How do you know about-- Who are you?
Were you that witness back then?

50:54.760 --> 50:57.888
Oh, no, that wasn't me.
Sorry, but that was actually your mother.

50:57.971 --> 51:00.682
Oh, right. You should also
look into his mother.

51:00.766 --> 51:01.767
Right, right.

51:03.060 --> 51:03.894
Huh?

51:11.026 --> 51:12.986
Are the police normally this friendly?

51:13.862 --> 51:15.072
They even gave me a coffee.

51:16.031 --> 51:18.533
Do you cause a lot of trouble
in the future? Here.

51:19.701 --> 51:22.746
To think that asshole and I
have the same condition.

51:23.580 --> 51:24.414
No.

51:25.248 --> 51:27.959
You're different.
That guy is just a killer.

51:29.669 --> 51:31.922
You're on my side? For real?

51:32.798 --> 51:34.549
Have we gotten close in the future?

51:35.258 --> 51:36.635
I guess you haven't killed me yet.

51:37.302 --> 51:38.178
Excuse me.

51:41.223 --> 51:43.266
Thank you so much. You saved me.

51:43.892 --> 51:46.937
If not for you, I'd be dead.
You're the reason I'm alive.

51:48.063 --> 51:50.524
-But I'm a psychopath, you know.
-Huh?

51:52.025 --> 51:53.610
-Ah.
-Mmm.

51:53.693 --> 51:57.364
Uh, then you're a psychopath
who saved my life.

51:58.156 --> 52:00.951
Thank you. I'll be grateful
for the rest of my life.

52:01.910 --> 52:03.578
Well, the cops need me to go back inside.

52:04.287 --> 52:06.373
Thank you again. Thank you.

52:07.082 --> 52:07.999
Thank you so much!

52:12.003 --> 52:14.548
Wow. No one's ever thanked me.

52:15.132 --> 52:16.216
I've never heard that.

52:18.426 --> 52:21.096
Wow. So no matter the day,

52:21.680 --> 52:23.849
all sorts of fun things happen
when we're together.

52:24.599 --> 52:25.725
Almost like the stars align.

52:27.894 --> 52:31.565
-Stars?
-Stars. I mean, the most unusual things.

52:31.648 --> 52:32.482
Oh!

52:34.484 --> 52:35.569
Hey.

52:36.862 --> 52:38.989
No, no. That's not what I meant.

52:39.072 --> 52:40.115
One minute.

52:43.535 --> 52:46.204
Hey, Min-ji, it's Ka-young.

52:46.288 --> 52:48.039
This guy almost killed a girl,

52:48.123 --> 52:50.709
but now another guy is spouting off
about the stars.

52:51.418 --> 52:53.628
Yeah, he's not a human. That's right.

52:54.379 --> 52:55.964
He's actually really not human.

52:57.340 --> 52:59.926
No. Right. You're right.

53:00.802 --> 53:02.888
Right, this is how you were.

53:02.971 --> 53:05.557
Hang on, I'm--
No, I'm not saying you're wrong.

53:07.017 --> 53:07.893
Ki Ka-young.

53:09.102 --> 53:11.771
I have to go now, to return to you.

53:12.314 --> 53:14.482
No. I'm not taking sides.

53:14.566 --> 53:16.067
'Cause watching you like this,

53:17.235 --> 53:18.570
I just miss you even more.

53:19.112 --> 53:20.947
Uh…

53:27.954 --> 53:28.872
Oh, no.

53:30.248 --> 53:31.416
But it's not raining.

53:31.958 --> 53:32.876
Shit.

53:44.262 --> 53:46.681
You acted like I was creepy,
and now you're asleep?

54:10.205 --> 54:12.707
You still fall for tricks like this?

54:13.375 --> 54:15.085
Well, you know…

54:15.877 --> 54:17.712
I wasn't trying to, that is--

54:32.394 --> 54:33.436
I swear to you.

54:34.562 --> 54:37.857
During all of your lost years,
the immortal flower lived on.

54:39.067 --> 54:40.026
I'll remember.

54:42.529 --> 54:43.363
What?

54:45.031 --> 54:45.907
You.

54:47.117 --> 54:48.201
Inside the lamp,

54:50.036 --> 54:51.997
of all the phrases you traced over,

54:53.081 --> 54:54.624
the one most often repeated…

55:04.843 --> 55:06.970
is habibti. That's it.

55:08.888 --> 55:10.890
And that means what?

55:14.811 --> 55:15.812
My true love.
